                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "27113fc6-342c-4f35-83eb-97418754f447",
                        "source_entry_id": "31e8fd4c-c02e-3669-883a-10378d2bb630",
                        "source_sense_id": "8c329320-69bc-3f6b-be9e-c6038f83f293",
                        "target_lang_word": "incognizable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "incognizable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2d17290-86b0-3f67-b7f1-02fe5171e18d",
                                        "entry_id": "448eba2b-1b68-3153-bd07-2863a0f111d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not cognizable; incapable of being recognised."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc06bf6f-eaae-42a3-9ad0-cc70943b7997",
                                                "sense_id": "d2d17290-86b0-3f67-b7f1-02fe5171e18d",
                                                "text": "1658, Thomas Saintserf (translator), Entertainments of the Cours: or, Academical Conversations, compiled by Melchior de Marmet, London, p. 104,\nA dead Body is always incognizable, not only because it is ordinarily changed, but because it neither speaks, nor acts; and for that the qualities of its Soul, which we should know, are departed with her, and have left nothing but a trunk, and a lump without motion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2300cd5-85ee-4e92-8e94-4e46900b2e7a",
                                                "sense_id": "d2d17290-86b0-3f67-b7f1-02fe5171e18d",
                                                "text": "The lettish race […] was not a primitive stock, as the finnish, the germanic, or slavonian, but a distinct branch, now become incognizable, of the Slavi […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0a719c2-e082-42d7-be4a-8bf609e52014",
                                                "sense_id": "d2d17290-86b0-3f67-b7f1-02fe5171e18d",
                                                "text": "[…] if therefore position is, to the nascent intelligence, incognizable except as the position of something that produces an impression on the organism; how is it possible for the idea of position ever to be dissociated from that of body?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33753bde-5651-4746-95f2-721db07749ae",
                                                "sense_id": "d2d17290-86b0-3f67-b7f1-02fe5171e18d",
                                                "text": "All this time the incognizable nouveau was smoking slowly and calmly, and looking at nothing at all with his black buttonlike eyes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dbac776a-2421-41e5-b8ef-8b2fa8c96595",
                        "source_entry_id": "31e8fd4c-c02e-3669-883a-10378d2bb630",
                        "source_sense_id": "8c329320-69bc-3f6b-be9e-c6038f83f293",
                        "target_lang_word": "unknowable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "unknowable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "533e7828-2298-30a9-a67e-d03d41c62265",
                                        "entry_id": "e66d0e63-a62b-3da1-b586-49e480dc151b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not knowable; not able to be known."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc2ef210-16f3-4653-a5fc-c90e2e242e73",
                                                "sense_id": "533e7828-2298-30a9-a67e-d03d41c62265",
                                                "text": "Number fourteen: Some of the things you need to know are things that are unknowable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92dbdd91-9852-4053-b455-61d696023fa2",
                                                "sense_id": "533e7828-2298-30a9-a67e-d03d41c62265",
                                                "text": "The mascot for the manosphere, Andrew Tate, believes that women belong at home, are a man’s property, and shouldn’t be able to drive. And an unknowable amount of young men are following this rhetoric through sites like Reddit, 4chan, and YouTube. But once they fall down the rabbit hole of the manosphere, is there any getting out?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "unknowable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba57d00a-e70c-38de-8e02-97c82d783650",
                                        "entry_id": "887bd742-e0f4-382e-aac3-963eaa8ff76b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that cannot be known."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63d55587-d5b7-4186-9150-c644e5a31e25",
                                                "sense_id": "ba57d00a-e70c-38de-8e02-97c82d783650",
                                                "text": "That night I think of other unknowables. How much love does one need in a lifetime? Is there a quantity of brain space that is allocated to love? And for those of us who have loved less, does this space become occupied by something else? Like cricket, or religion, perhaps."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8baac619-af73-41fb-a7af-d116cc68936c",
                        "source_entry_id": "31e8fd4c-c02e-3669-883a-10378d2bb630",
                        "source_sense_id": "8c329320-69bc-3f6b-be9e-c6038f83f293",
                        "target_lang_word": "inscrutable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inscrutable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f245990a-36ea-309c-9df5-e7b4cc16213e",
                                        "entry_id": "721596fe-e922-37fb-b5a9-5bf0195b711a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Difficult or impossible to comprehend, fathom, or interpret."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf604419-de3d-4566-aaf8-89a4ba7b4469",
                                                "sense_id": "f245990a-36ea-309c-9df5-e7b4cc16213e",
                                                "text": "His inscrutable theories would years later become the foundation of a whole new science."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06ade488-6c09-4419-956e-2a0123d5bf1d",
                                                "sense_id": "f245990a-36ea-309c-9df5-e7b4cc16213e",
                                                "text": "The pale, inscrutable determinateness, and flinchless intrepidity of Pierre, now began to domineer upon them; for any social unusualness or greatness is sometimes most impressive in the retrospect."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de5def77-e3c3-464b-b997-5972a96898ab",
                                                "sense_id": "f245990a-36ea-309c-9df5-e7b4cc16213e",
                                                "text": "It was unconscious, this smile was, though just after he had said something it got intensified for an instant. It came at the end of his speeches like a seal applied on the words to make the meaning of the commonest phrase appear absolutely inscrutable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98f6ab16-5fb8-4f86-bad7-f9e68d54148b",
                                                "sense_id": "f245990a-36ea-309c-9df5-e7b4cc16213e",
                                                "text": "She called my vanity license plate inscrutable! 'ICU81MI'? Hilarious!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e56580a9-410d-448d-814a-f4d9e4517ae4",
                                                "sense_id": "f245990a-36ea-309c-9df5-e7b4cc16213e",
                                                "text": "The writer Juan Rulfo, whose 1955 novel, “Pedro Páramo,” still stands as the central monument of modern Mexican literature, grew up in Jalisco and vividly depicted its arid, sun-blasted landscapes in his writing, while the architect Luis Barragán, who moved from Guadalajara to Mexico City in the 1930s, carried with him an appreciation for his home state’s cloisters, haciendas and humble country buildings, which he translated in his own work as austere, inscrutable volumes of stucco."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "inscrutable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a97a8ef0-12d7-3c28-9cfa-46701e43f0a5",
                                        "entry_id": "5ecfa31a-3789-30d6-938a-a6a5bc58655c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who or that which is inscrutable; a person, etc. that cannot be comprehended."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0c1c1aa1-8c99-491b-b02a-50d7d663e562",
                        "source_entry_id": "31e8fd4c-c02e-3669-883a-10378d2bb630",
                        "source_sense_id": "8c329320-69bc-3f6b-be9e-c6038f83f293",
                        "target_lang_word": "impenetrable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "impenetrable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a0e1d2b-5e54-39f1-83c9-8802678162a9",
                                        "entry_id": "95a23609-cfdb-3bba-ba76-7f548afb8cc7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not penetrable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "125b5a82-5814-4ef8-8f29-5dd900064a3e",
                                                "sense_id": "6a0e1d2b-5e54-39f1-83c9-8802678162a9",
                                                "text": "The fortress is impenetrable, so it cannot be taken."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "868735ea-6d28-47bf-a2cc-8137416d8d5f",
                                                "sense_id": "6a0e1d2b-5e54-39f1-83c9-8802678162a9",
                                                "text": "The avalanche spread and stopped, locking everything it carried into an icy cocoon. It was now a jagged, virtually impenetrable pile of ice, longer than a football field and nearly as wide."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea5dee9f-3d38-30a0-b452-4dc8d55bd5fb",
                                        "entry_id": "95a23609-cfdb-3bba-ba76-7f548afb8cc7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Opaque; obscure; not translucent or transparent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88793df9-b1e9-4e0f-aa71-57a24bc690bb",
                                                "sense_id": "ea5dee9f-3d38-30a0-b452-4dc8d55bd5fb",
                                                "text": "When night falls, she cloaks the world in impenetrable darkness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2acf5aad-4295-3574-b224-4bb266678555",
                                        "entry_id": "95a23609-cfdb-3bba-ba76-7f548afb8cc7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Incomprehensible; fathomless; inscrutable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b4b9b53-3cfc-4b5e-98df-be92d3ce4e4a",
                                                "sense_id": "2acf5aad-4295-3574-b224-4bb266678555",
                                                "text": "Business jargon makes this document impenetrable—I can’t understand it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "impenetrable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ebbccfe1-9ccf-3ddb-8f85-22defc2ad3c0",
                                        "entry_id": "27fb4cc9-420a-3f56-8b57-c32440f17942",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person not openly given to friendship."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28c99ddd-bbf5-4ed2-a485-bb9f5cd85523",
                                                "sense_id": "ebbccfe1-9ccf-3ddb-8f85-22defc2ad3c0",
                                                "text": "I should lose the reputation that I am gradually acquiring among our impenetrables here, were I to confess the excitement which I felt at the idea of entering his house—the house of that great general under whose command you made your first charge."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
